  <page_number>107</page_number>
  <running_head>LYRICA.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <p>
    <i>Et paruum culicem, leuésque nugas.</i>
    <i>Luxit carmine passerem Catullus</i>
    <i>Extinctum querulo sua puella.</i>
    <i>Sic suetam liceat dolere ficum</i>
    <i>Nobis nectareas referre ficos,</i>
    <i>Atque umbras dare frondibus venustis</i>
    <i>(Dum vixit) virides, vigente sole</i>
    <i>Quid? si commoda pensitare mecum</i>
    <i>Mente cuncta voles serenior,</i>
    <i>Quae ficus mea proferebat olim,</i>
    <i>Hic me ludere fortiter negabis:</i>
    <i>Nec fictas lachrymas meas putabis.</i>
    </p>
    <p>
    <i>Quae te frigore perculit</i>
    <i>Tanto bruma ferox? Quis Boreas gelu</i>
    <i>Nuper Sarmatico furens</i>
    <i>Te, Ficus, stygias iussit ad arbores</i>
    <i>Migrare: atque Proserpinae</i>
    <i>Lucos examinem visere luridos,</i>
    <i>Et furuas Erebi domos:</i>
    <i>Atque horrenda nigris antra paludibus?</i>
    <i>Extinctas precor, o, precor</i>
    <i>Nostri delitias, Pieris, hortuli</i>
    <i>Moesto squallida carmine</i>
    <i>Dic, &amp; perpetuis obrue fletibus.</i>
    <i>Priscis non fuit hortulis</i>
    <i>Arbos Hesperidum dignior aspici,</i>
    <i>Auro tergeminis licet</i>
    <i>Diui fulua darent poma sororibus</i>
    </p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The verse lines are set as printed; the italic long s is rendered as s. The page is a clean page of verse with no marginal notes.</notes>
